Package: jitsi-audio-bridge
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), libopus0, init-system-helpers (>= 1.18)
Recommends: ffmpeg
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Description: record Jitsi participant audio and email a transcript
 Captures per-participant Opus audio from a Jitsi Videobridge over a
 WebSocket, records each participant to a WAV file, then transcribes it with a
 Whisper endpoint, summarises it with an Ollama endpoint and emails the
 result. The same pipeline also runs over recordings that already exist on
 disk.
 .
 The package carries its own dependencies in a private virtualenv under
 /usr/lib/jitsi-audio-bridge, because the distribution's python3-websockets
 is older than the websockets>=13 this daemon requires. That virtualenv was
 built for python3 @PYTHON_MINOR@, so build and install on the same
 distribution.
